 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is retried with growing pauses; [the capture implementation](../../larder/capture.py)
+defines the attempt limit and pause lengths.
+
+During the gateway's Friday peak, 17:00 to 19:00, slow responses left 58 confirmed pantry orders uncharged. A
+volunteer captured them by hand the following morning. The previous three attempts ran back to back within a
+second, landing in the same slow period. In a sandbox replay, five attempts spaced 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds apart would
+have recovered 57 of those 58 captures. The team accepted up to 20 seconds of additional waiting on the confirmation
+page to reduce manual captures. Switching gateways was deferred because the contract runs to December 2026. These
+findings and the accepted trade-off came from [issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md).
 
